{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/prf-parity-regime-selection","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Proof","doco:Section"],"label":"prf:parity-regime-selection","kind":"proof","title":"Proof of parity regime selection","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/thm-parity-regime-selection"],"text":"parity-regime-selection-proof.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"prf:parity-regime-selection\"></a>\n<strong>Proof.</strong> <em>Proof of parity regime selection</em></p>\n<h2>Proof</h2>\n<p>Since <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a &#x3C; 0</code> and <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">b &#x3C; 0</code> for all <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q > 1</code> (<a href=\"#def:spectator-normalization\">spectator normalization</a>), the product <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">a^Z \\cdot b^{N-1}</code> carries the sign <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(-1)^Z \\cdot (-1)^{N-1} = (-1)^{A-1}</code>.</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Odd <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code></strong>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(-1)^{A-1} = +1</code>. The factorization is positive.</li>\n<li><strong>Even <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code></strong>: <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(-1)^{A-1} = -1</code>. The factorization is negative, so the raw character sum fails to yield <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Q > 0</code> directly.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The even-<code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code> case requires restricting to Frobenius-positive configurations (<a href=\"#prop:confinement-lp\">confinement LP</a>). This constraint ensures that both parent and daughter exhibit non-negative Markov traces.</p>\n<h2>Numerical verification</h2>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Decay</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">A</code></th>\n<th>Regime</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Q_{\\mathrm{calc}}</code> (MeV)</th>\n<th><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">Q_{\\mathrm{exp}}</code> (MeV)</th>\n<th>Error</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">n \\to p</code></td>\n<td>1 (odd)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(S\\Delta+1) \\times m_e</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 0.7816</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.7823</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-0.10\\%</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^3\\mathrm{H} \\to {}^3\\mathrm{He}</code></td>\n<td>3 (odd)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\|S\\Delta\\| \\times m_e</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 0.0179</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">0.0186</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">-3.64\\%</code></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">{}^6\\mathrm{He} \\to {}^6\\mathrm{Li}</code></td>\n<td>6 (even)</td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">(\\Sigma_{\\mathrm{FP}}+1) \\times m_e</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\approx 3.637</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3.508</code></td>\n<td><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">+3.68\\%</code></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n"}
